{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: repair the remaining semantic inconsistencies in the runnable work-loop guide as a companion to #20305. This child adds one how-to-page outcome to the existing AGENTS/SKILL editorial commission. Keep full I7 and earlier commitments first; handle it with the #20305 editorial pass when practical, accounting for both commitments and exact changed paths. Do not interrupt active work or duplicate another owner.\n\nIn the [current runnable guide](docs/how-to/run-a-work-loop.md@3ecb8b77d55cfe8ccb1d634649788a4ab629577b:58), the first artifact claims make test and make vet pass although neither command runs and the scratch project contains only a changelog. Replace that claim with verification the example actually performs; preserve the adjacent instruction to report only evidence actually obtained.\n\nThe [withdrawal example](docs/how-to/run-a-work-loop.md@3ecb8b77d55cfe8ccb1d634649788a4ab629577b:118) seals the changelog merge, then promises a parser rewrite on the already satisfied changelog request. Show withdrawal from a separately assigned, still unfinished request with explicit conditions and the appropriate destination instead. Do not teach a promise to widen an unrelated outcome or imply that withdrawing a promise retires the underlying request. Keep the original changelog completion intact. Make the [discovered-work example](docs/how-to/run-a-work-loop.md@3ecb8b77d55cfe8ccb1d634649788a4ab629577b:146) chronologically coherent with its narrative, preserving the already corrected target inheritance for a source-bearing child. A small reorder or clearly independent scenario is preferable to extra workflow machinery.\n\nThe [audit evidence](runloop-evidence.json) includes current native ownership, byte-equal live bases and the limits of the earlier passing example run. The [runner](internal/docset/examples_test.go@3ecb8b77d55cfe8ccb1d634649788a4ab629577b:96) executes all shell blocks in order and checks exit status; successful commands al